--TEST--
The route table's seven contradictions, refused in one compilation — `rule:routing/path-grammar`, `rule:security/route-capture-is-laundered-by-its-type` and `rule:routing/link-name-and-params-are-checked` and `rule:routing/a-query-parameter-is-declared-like-a-capture`, `rule:routing/a-trailing-segment-may-be-absent` and `rule:routing/a-leftover-link-key-is-a-query-string`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// Seven wrong route declarations in one program, because the point is not that
// each is refused — the unit tests in `crates/nvs-types/tests/routes.rs` ask
// that one at a time — but that the table reports *all* of them from one
// compilation rather than stopping at the first. A pass that aborted after the
// duplicate would look identical on any single-error case.

// 1. `rule:routing/path-grammar`: a path is matched by shape, so two rows claiming one path
// and one verb are one route declared twice, whatever their names.
class Dup {
    #[Core\Route(path: "/dup", method: Core\Http\Method::Get, name: "dup.first")]
    #[Core\Access(allow: Core\Audience::Public)]
    public function first(): string { return ""; }

    #[Core\Route(path: "/dup", method: Core\Http\Method::Get, name: "dup.second")]
    #[Core\Access(allow: Core\Audience::Public)]
    public function second(): string { return ""; }
}

// 2. `rule:security/route-capture-is-laundered-by-its-type`: every capture has somewhere to arrive, and the method that
// declares no parameter at all is the shortest way to have nowhere.
class Unbound {
    #[Core\Route(path: "/users/{id}", method: Core\Http\Method::Get, name: "unbound.show")]
    #[Core\Access(allow: Core\Audience::Public)]
    public function show(): string { return ""; }
}

// 3. `rule:routing/a-trailing-segment-may-be-absent`: `{name?}` matches one segment or none, and "or none" only
// has an answer where nothing follows it.
class Middle {
    #[Core\Route(path: "/posts/{page?}/comments", method: Core\Http\Method::Get, name: "middle.show")]
    #[Core\Access(allow: Core\Audience::Public)]
    public function show(uint $page = 1): string { return ""; }
}

// 4. `rule:routing/a-trailing-segment-may-be-absent` again, and the refusal is about the *default* rather than the
// type: the default is what makes the absent segment well-typed.
class NoDefault {
    #[Core\Route(path: "/drafts/{page?}", method: Core\Http\Method::Get, name: "nodefault.page")]
    #[Core\Access(allow: Core\Audience::Public)]
    public function page(uint $page): string { return ""; }
}

// 5. `rule:routing/a-query-parameter-is-declared-like-a-capture` is a closed list, and `float` is the first type outside it a
// language that guesses would have converted.
class BadType {
    #[Core\Route(path: "/items/{id}", method: Core\Http\Method::Get, name: "badtype.show")]
    #[Core\Access(allow: Core\Audience::Public)]
    public function show(float $id): string { return ""; }
}

// The one well-formed row. The two link errors below are asked against it, so
// that neither of them is really a complaint about the route.
class Orders {
    #[Core\Route(path: "/orders/{id}", method: Core\Http\Method::Get, name: "orders.show")]
    #[Core\Access(allow: Core\Audience::Public)]
    public function show(uint $id, #[Core\Query] uint $page = 1): string { return ""; }
}

// 6. `rule:routing/link-name-and-params-are-checked`: a *literal* name is checked against the compiled table. A
// computed one is not checked here at all and throws at run time instead.
echo Core\Router::url("orders.missing", ["id" => 1]), "\n";

// 7. `rule:routing/a-leftover-link-key-is-a-query-string`: every key that is not a capture becomes the link's query
// string, so a misspelling ships as `?pge=2` and nothing says so — which is why
// this could not be refused before `#[Query]` said which keys are legitimate.
echo Core\Router::url("orders.show", ["id" => 1, "pge" => 2]), "\n";

echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0748]: `Get /dup` is already served by `Dup::first`
   --> case.nvs:15:7
%A
error[E0751]: `Unbound::show` has no parameter `$id` for `{id}` to arrive as
   --> case.nvs:23:18
%A
error[E0750]: `Middle::show`'s path writes `{page?}` somewhere other than the last position
   --> case.nvs:31:18
%A
error[E0753]: `$page` has no default, so `{page?}` has nothing to be when it is absent
   --> case.nvs:39:18
%A
error[E0752]: `float` is not a type `{id}` can arrive at
   --> case.nvs:47:18
%A
error[E0754]: `Core\Router::url` names the route `orders.missing`, and no `#[Route]` claims it
   --> case.nvs:62:23
%A
error[E0759]: `Orders::show`'s path `/orders/{id}` has no `pge`, and `Orders::show` declares no `#[Query]` parameter of that name
   --> case.nvs:67:6
%A
